GIVETH A LIST OF `Row of the table in section 5(1)`
`the table in section 5(1)` MEANS
    LIST
        `s 5(1) row 1`
      , `s 5(1) row 2`
      , `s 5(1) row 3`
      , `s 5(1) row 4`
      , `s 5(1) row 5`
      , `s 5(1) row 6`
      , `s 5(1) row 7`
      , `s 5(1) row 8`
      , `s 5(1) row 9`
      , `s 5(1) row 10`
      , `s 5(1) row 11`
      , `s 5(1) row 12`
      , `s 5(1) row 13`
      , `s 5(1) row 14`
      , `s 5(1) row 15`
      , `s 5(1) row 16`

GIVEN `the word in column 1` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `Row of the table in section 5(1)`
`the row of the table for` MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (`has this column 1`) `the table in section 5(1)`
        WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `the first` FOLLOWED BY `the rest` THEN JUST `the first`
    WHERE
        `has this column 1` row MEANS row's `column 1` EQUALS `the word in column 1`

-- A reference within the ambit of column 1 has effect as the corresponding reference in column 2:
-- a person registered under the National Law to practise in that profession, other than as a student where the row says so,
-- and in the division the row names where it names one.
-- src:250 | (1) A reference in an Act or a legislative instrument within the ambit of column 1 of the following table will have effect as if it were the corresponding reference in column 2 of the table.
@ref s 5(1) (src:250)
GIVEN `the word in column 1` IS A STRING
      `the person is registered under the National Law to practise in that profession` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is registered only as a student` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is registered in the division the row names` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person is within a reference in column 1 of the table` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the row of the table for` `the word in column 1`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST row THEN
            JUST (    `the person is registered under the National Law to practise in that profession`
                  AND (IF row's `students are excluded` THEN (NOT `the person is registered only as a student`) ELSE TRUE)
                  AND (IF row's `a division is required` THEN `the person is registered in the division the row names` ELSE TRUE))

-- src:269 | (2) A reference in an Act or a legislative instrument to a registered health practitioner will have effect as if it were a reference to a health practitioner registered in the relevant health profession under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law.
@ref s 5(2) (src:269)
GIVEN `the person is a health practitioner registered in the relevant health profession under the National Law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person is within a reference to a registered health practitioner` MEANS
    `the person is a health practitioner registered in the relevant health profession under the National Law`

GIVEN `the word in column 1` IS A STRING, `the words in column 2` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the row of the table has this column 2` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the row of the table for` `the word in column 1`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST row THEN row's `column 2` EQUALS `the words in column 2`

§§ `Tests`

#ASSERT count `the table in section 5(1)` EQUALS 16
#ASSERT `the row of the table has this column 2` "chiropractor" "a person registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law to practise in the chiropractic profession (other than as a student)"
#ASSERT `the row of the table has this column 2` "dental practitioner" "a person registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law to practise in the dental profession (including, if appropriate, a dental therapist, dental hygienist, dental prosthetist or oral health therapist but not including a student)"
#ASSERT `the row of the table has this column 2` "dentist" "a person registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law— (a)	to practise in the dental profession as a dentist (other than as a student); and (b)	in the dentists division of that profession"
#ASSERT `the row of the table has this column 2` "enrolled nurse" "a person registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law— (a)	to practise in the nursing profession as a nurse (other than as a student); and (b)	in the enrolled nurses division of that profession"
#ASSERT `the row of the table has this column 2` "legally qualified medical practitioner" "a person registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law to practise in the medical profession (other than as a student)"
#ASSERT `the row of the table has this column 2` "medical practitioner" "a person registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law to practise in the medical profession (other than as a student)"
#ASSERT `the row of the table has this column 2` "midwife" "a person registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law to practise in the midwifery profession as a midwife (other than as a student)"
#ASSERT `the row of the table has this column 2` "nurse" "a person registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law to practise in the nursing profession as a nurse (other than as a student)"
#ASSERT `the row of the table has this column 2` "occupational therapist" "a person registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law to practise in the occupational therapy profession (other than as a student)"
#ASSERT `the row of the table has this column 2` "optometrist" "a person registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law to practise in the optometry profession (other than as a student)"
#ASSERT `the row of the table has this column 2` "osteopath" "a person registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law to practise in the osteopathy profession (other than as a student)"
#ASSERT `the row of the table has this column 2` "pharmacist" "a person registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law to practise in the pharmacy profession (other than as a student)"
#ASSERT `the row of the table has this column 2` "physiotherapist" "a person registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law to practise in the physiotherapy profession (other than as a student)"
#ASSERT `the row of the table has this column 2` "podiatrist" "a person registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law to practise in the podiatry profession (other than as a student)"
#ASSERT `the row of the table has this column 2` "psychologist" "a person registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law to practise in the psychology profession (other than as a student)"
#ASSERT `the row of the table has this column 2` "registered nurse" "a person registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law— (a)	to practise in the nursing profession as a nurse (other than as a student); and (b)	in the registered nurses division of that profession"
#ASSERT `the row of the table for` "bailiff" EQUALS NOTHING
-- chiropractor: registered to practise in the chiropractic profession (other than as a student).
#ASSERT `a person is within a reference in column 1 of the table` "chiropractor" TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a person is within a reference in column 1 of the table` "chiropractor" TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a person is within a reference in column 1 of the table` "chiropractor" FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- dentist: the dentists division is also required.
#ASSERT `a person is within a reference in column 1 of the table` "dentist" TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a person is within a reference in column 1 of the table` "dentist" TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- dental practitioner: no division is required, and students are not included.
#ASSERT `a person is within a reference in column 1 of the table` "dental practitioner" TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a person is within a reference in column 1 of the table` "dental practitioner" TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- nurse needs no division; enrolled nurse and registered nurse each need theirs.
#ASSERT `a person is within a reference in column 1 of the table` "nurse" TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a person is within a reference in column 1 of the table` "enrolled nurse" TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a person is within a reference in column 1 of the table` "enrolled nurse" TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a person is within a reference in column 1 of the table` "registered nurse" TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- midwife: the profession is the midwifery profession; no division.
#ASSERT `a person is within a reference in column 1 of the table` "midwife" TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A word not in column 1 is outside the table.
#ASSERT `a person is within a reference in column 1 of the table` "bailiff" TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a person is within a reference to a registered health practitioner` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a person is within a reference to a registered health practitioner` FALSE)
